\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S9}{\ignorespaces \stale {router_grid}{} Change of the cost saving per tonne-kilometre, in points, against the reference, stages \SI {30}{nmi} and rows \SI {7.5}{nmi} apart with every time step halved, for the \SI {140}{m} e-ammonia ship to Guadeloupe with a kite and with rotors: the mean over 12 departures with its standard error, the change of the kite's gap to the rotors, and the computing time of one rig's 12 round trips. The plan keeps every fourth row beyond the first \SI {240}{nmi}, to the end unless graded, and the time steps are those of the results unless scaled with the grid; the whole corridor is searched at once in the last row. Times come from runs on a shared machine, so ratios under about 1.2 are not firm. Development runs of 2026-11-14 and 15, commits 4c05b87 to 2b0e5e5.}}{27}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
